Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos8895: reserve SM-G955N secure camera RAM

Samsung's dream2lte reserved-memory layout places the secure camera
carveout at 0xd0000000 for 20 MiB. Keep it out of the Linux allocator
and linear map on the Korean board. R58 included this interval in
System RAM and reported an asynchronous abort while the page allocator
was clearing a page consistent with an address inside the carveout.

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/exynos8895-dream2lteks.dts
@@ -54,6 +54,11 @@
 
 		framebuffer@cc000000 {
 			reg = <0 0xcc000000 (1440 * 2960 * 4)>;
+			no-map;
+		};
+
+		secure-camera@d0000000 {
+			reg = <0 0xd0000000 0x1400000>;
 			no-map;
 		};
 	};
